    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_198f8fb9",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: rare_picture_of_child_birth; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image shows a baby in a diaper standing on a kitchen floor, facing an open dishwasher. The overlaid text reads \"rare picture of child birth,\" which is a deliberate and absurd mislabeling. This juxtaposition creates a humorous, yet misleading, visual pun. The intent is to shock or amuse by creating a false equivalence between a mundane, everyday scene (a baby exploring a dishwasher) and a major life event (childbirth). While not overtly abusive, hateful, or propagandistic, the meme's harmfulness lies in its potential to trivialize or misrepresent the profound experience of childbirth, reducing it to a joke. The humor is derived from the absurdity of the comparison, which may be insensitive to those who have experienced childbirth, potentially causing emotional discomfort or reinforcing a dismissive attitude toward the event. The meme does not target any specific protected group but uses a misleading analogy to generate humor, which can be considered harmful due to its potential to trivialize a significant human experience.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_3faded31"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
